The best interval we can use (the interval whose points are given that's closest to $x=4$) is the interval between $x=3$ and $x=5$. Let's find the average rate of change between those points.

$\begin{align}
f'(4)&\approx\dfrac{f(5)-f(3)}{5-3}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{112-95}{2}
\\\\
&=8.5
\end{align}$
